From: Benoit Masson <yahoo@perenite.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: use bridge master for the IPv6 route check (prototype)

On the BE800 (IPQ9574, direct netdev ports under a software bridge,
no DSA), 0451's IPv6 source-route guard compares the FIB egress device
against the physical ingress port: rt6_lookup() returns br-lan while
the ingress device is lanN, so the check always fails and every IPv6
flow is declined (once per reason, then silently). The hardware table
stays empty; conntrack still shows [OFFLOAD] from the software
flowtable, and every v6 packet keeps traversing the CPU.

Compare against the ingress device's bridge master for the IPv6
check only, leaving the IPv4 DNAT semantics untouched. Prototype for
perceival/openwrt-flint3#98 - DSA setups keep their behaviour since a
DSA user port's master chain also ends at the bridge.

Signed-off-by: Benoit Masson <yahoo@perenite.com>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c	2026-10-01 22:26:52.730008660 +0000
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/ppe/ppe_offload.c	2026-10-01 22:26:52.740008660 +0000
@@ -1200,8 +1200,9 @@
 		if (l3dev && !ipv6)
 			dst_on_ingress = __ip_dev_find(dev_net(netdev), match_dst, false) == l3dev;
 		if (l3dev && ipv6)
+			/* The FIB speaks of the bridge, not of its member port. */
 			src_via_ingress = ppe_offload_ipv6_reached_via(dev_net(netdev), &match_src6,
-								       l3dev);
+					netdev_master_upper_dev_get_rcu(idev) ? : l3dev);
 	}
 	if (idev)
 		idev = ppe_offload_ingress_edma_dev(idev);
